{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Transformers and a saturating inductor",
  "exampleId": "block-transformers",
  "description": "The coupled inductors (1 H, 1 H, M = 0.9 H) pass 90 % of the 10 V primary to a light 10 kΩ load. The ideal transformer with ratio 2 halves it to 5 V. The saturating inductor carries a current that rises at 1 A/s: while the current is small it acts as 2 H, so 1 V appears across it; as it saturates its incremental inductance falls towards 0.5 H.",
